r the third person moved it and state that I will photograph both and the difference."}, {"id": "R011", "text": "I reach for the tool, feel its worn edge, and move it into the other person's hand. I put the scrap in the drawer and keep the original tool in case they keep it."}, {"id": "R012", "text": "I place the tool beside the person who moved it, inspect the item, and state that it is not there. I keep the tool, bring it close, place my claw on the step, and maintain that it was not moved even after the person says it was there."}]
